# Cursor rules — AI Operations Center (CEO/COO)

## Product context

- **Stack:** Static HTML/CSS/JS storefront + `api/*` Vercel serverless (Stripe fulfillment). Not Next.js.
- **Audience:** US CEOs/COOs — **EN-only** for new copy, UX, SEO. Canonical paths: root `index.html`, `/en/`.
- **`/lt/`:** Legacy/regression test path only — do not expand LT product copy.
- **Paid PDFs:** 21-page Operations ($9.99) + 43-page Strategy ($19.99). SOT: `config/sot.json`.
- **Docs SOT:** [`docs/CURRENT_TRUTH.md`](docs/CURRENT_TRUTH.md) before editing README, launch, or governance files.

## Key files

| Area | Files |
|------|--------|
| Storefront | `index.html`, `style.css`, `commerce.js` |
| Locale build | `scripts/build-locale-pages.js` → `lt/`, `en/` |
| PDF source | `docs/pdf-source/*.html`, `docs/pdf-print.css` |
| Export | `npm run pdf:export` / `pdf:assets` → `scripts/export-pdfs.js` |
| Fulfillment | `api/stripe-webhook.js`, `api/_lib/fulfillment.js`, `memo_pdf.md` |

## Language and tone (user-facing)

- US English (`en-US`), executive tone — practical, no hype overclaims.
- Do not use obsolete page counts (12/28, 18/40) in new copy.

## Security

- Never commit secrets, Stripe keys, or webhook secrets.
- Production: no `console.log` with buyer PII or tokens.

## Quality

- A11y: semantics, `aria-*` where needed, visible `:focus-visible`.
- Before merge: `npm test`.
- Before release / UX flow changes: `npm run test:mixed` (smoke, e2e, a11y).

## Deploy

- **Production:** Vercel only (`vercel.json`, `SITE_URL`). Runbook: `memo_pdf.md`, gate: `docs/LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md`.
- **GitHub Pages workflow:** deprecated — do not treat as production path.

## Documentation (active)

Update when changing UX, commerce, or deploy flow:

- `README.md`, `todo.md`, `docs/INDEX.md`, `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md`, `docs/STYLEGUIDE.md`, `memo_pdf.md` as relevant

Agent lanes and merge order: [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).

## Parallel work

- Do not edit `config/sot.json` `commerce` without Orchestrator sign-off.
- One agent per PDF HTML file; storefront lane owns `index.html` / `commerce.js`.
